# Secrets and environment. Never commit these.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.secret
secrets/
*.key
# The cross-impl conformance FIXTURE key is synthetic test data, not a secret: the
# engine generator mints a throwaway identity purely so the Go reader can prove it
# opens an engine-sealed export byte-identically. Without this exception the *.key
# rule silently drops it and TestUnsealExportConformance fails on every clean clone.
!cmd/downpipe/testdata/sealed-export/identity.key
*.pem
*.age

# Conformance fixtures are the exception: the break-glass identity and any other
# key material under the vector corpus is published test data, not a live secret, so
# the reader can replay it. Without this negation a plain "git add" would silently
# drop every new vector's identity.key and the vector would fail only on a clean CI
# checkout (the dir looks complete locally). The narrow path keeps real keys ignored.
!internal/format/testdata/vectors/**/*.key
# The custody fixtures are the same class: a throwaway identity, its wrapped envelope
# and the Shamir shares over its wrapping key, generated so the offline recombine path
# is proven byte-compatible with the artefacts the console emits. The *.key rule would
# silently drop expected-identity.key and the conformance tests would fail only on a
# clean clone.
!cmd/downpipe/testdata/custody/**
# The cross-impl conformance FIXTURE key is synthetic test data, not a secret: the
# engine generator mints a throwaway identity purely so the Go reader can prove it
# opens an engine-sealed export byte-identically. Without this exception the *.key
# rule silently drops it and TestUnsealExportConformance fails on every clean clone.
!cmd/downpipe/testdata/sealed-export/identity.key
!internal/format/testdata/vectors/**/*.pem
!internal/format/testdata/vectors/**/*.age

# Build output
/dist/
/build/
*.exe
*.test

# Coverage
coverage.out
coverage.txt
/coverage/

# Go workspace
go.work
go.work.sum

# IDE and editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local scratch
/tmp/

# compiled CLI binary
/downpipe
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Node deps for the ajv schema validator (scripts/schema-validate); the pinned
# package-lock.json is committed and `npm ci` restores them in CI.
node_modules/

# Ignore a node_modules SYMLINK as well as a node_modules directory. The rule above ends in "/",
# which git matches against directories only, and a linked git worktree can link node_modules at the
# primary checkout rather than installing a second copy of it. Without this bare line the link
# shows up as untracked and a stray `git add -A` commits an absolute, machine-local path.
node_modules
